Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Enhancing Group Theory Capabilities in Mathematica", "Title",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9651014891010036`*^9, 3.9651015044263554`*^9}, 
   3.966775555019331*^9},ExpressionUUID->"d69f2dcf-b5a4-8243-9c69-\
667ac87cac3e"],

Cell["\<\
Authors : Jules Charlier, Oscar Eatwell, Jawad Ben Brahim, Rafael Salavarria \
Lorenzoni
\
\>", "Subtitle",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9667755693662148`*^9, 
  3.9667756021752853`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"4148549f-16ef-414b-8ac3-\
2291c3467070"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Introduction", "Chapter",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.966775609057722*^9, 
  3.9667756125877075`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"3aeadb11-59db-9d4e-9f4f-\
f6a1ac22c02d"],

Cell["\<\
This project extends the group theory capabilities of Mathematica by \
providing additional functions to work with groups, monoids, and magmas. It \
includes tools for identifying group attributes, generating Cayley \
multiplication tables, testing structural properties (abelian, center, \
identity), and exploring algebraic examples.

The aim is both educational and exploratory: to make it easier for students \
and researchers to experiment with algebraic structures using the Wolfram \
Language.
\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.9667756261921406`*^9, 
  3.9667762963187695`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"2ce05db1-7f6e-d647-b365-\
08609fd4fed5"]
}, Open  ]],

